qACAkV9wYnwFonaA4s_yYr5BXdI21vtgJw8BXe8lKn_w==\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Formatting clinical picture**\\n\\nI need to start by delivering the answer in the Clinical Picture Output Structure. I think I should also include the Recommended Questions section but only provide the first question. It might be a good idea to fetch information from KLM and mention any red flags like exhaustion or worsening symptoms over months. While there’s no obvious emergency from this info, I’ll emphasize that any chest pain would be urgent. Let's format it properly for the user!\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] **Current clinical picture**\nI pulled your stored record and genomics before answering. From your EHR/DNA context, I see a history of **hypertension**, later noted as **uncontrolled**, plus **chronic kidney disease stage 2** with prior kidney markers showing **eGFR around 71** and **UACR around 135**; your record also lists **lisinopril 20 mg** and **amlodipine 5 mg**. What is new from you today is **progressively worsening exhaustion over the last few months**, which could be relevant in the setting of blood pressure treatment, kidney disease, sleep issues, anemia, thyroid/metabolic causes, or less specific chronic stress/inflammation.\n\n**Preliminary interpretation**\nAt this stage, the more supported possibilities include **fatigue related to chronic medical factors already in your record** such as blood pressure disease, kidney disease burden, medication effects, or poor sleep quality. Other common explanations that would still need to be separated out include **anemia**, **thyroid problems**, **low mood/stress overload**, **infection/inflammation**, or less commonly a heart-related cause if you also have shortness of breath, swelling, chest symptoms, or reduced exercise tolerance. Your DNA data may support a tendency toward hypertension/CKD progression, but it does **not by itself explain new exhaustion**, so the current symptom pattern matters most. If you are also having **chest pain, fainting, severe shortness of breath, black stools, or rapidly worsening weakness**, that would make this more urgent.\n\n**Recommended questions**\nIf you answer a few targeted questions, I can narrow this down much better.\n\n**(1/5)** When during the day is the exhaustion worst, and has it changed your sleep, exercise tolerance, concentration, or ability to do normal activities?","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_027b4c2e56826ffb0169d8fb4d41088191935c74cc17d7a26b\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":9542,"output":442,"cacheRead":13824,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":23808,"cost":{"input":0.023855,"output":0.0066300000000000005,"cacheRead":0.003456,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.033941}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1775827783823}}
