he attached text.\n\nWhat I need from you:\n1) A concise but meaningful differential diagnosis ranked/grouped.\n2) How the kidney history, hypertension history, rare pink urine, and fever/weight loss alter concern.\n3) Whether the wearable snapshot changes the assessment much.\n4) Immediate safety guidance for the patient.\n5) Keep it suitable for direct relay to the patient on Telegram."},"partialJson":"{\"label\":\"doctor-agent-diagnosis\",\"runtime\":\"subagent\",\"mode\":\"run\",\"cleanup\":\"delete\",\"cwd\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-patient-agent\",\"task\":\"You are LoopAI Doctor Agent, a specialized diagnostic support agent. Review this case and return a patient-facing diagnostic assessment in clear structured language. Do not claim certainty. Distinguish record-grounded facts from interpretation. Include red flags and suggested next diagnostic direction. \\n\\nPatient context from KLM/EHR/DNA (patient PT-8839-CR):\\n- 48-year-old male\\n- Hypertension; later uncontrolled hypertension\\n- CKD stage 2\\n- Prior BP 158/98 on 2025-10-10\\n- Prior kidney markers: eGFR 71, UACR 135\\n- Medications in record: lisinopril 20 mg, amlodipine 5 mg\\n- Genomics/risk context: ACE rs4340 D/D, AGT rs699 T/T, APOL1 rs73885319 G/G, NOS3 rs1799983 T/T, UMOD rs4293393 A/A; high PRS for hypertension and CKD progression\\n\\nCurrent user-reported symptoms:\\n- Exhaustion worsening over months\\n- Worse in evening\\n- Reduced exercise tolerance\\n- Some shortness of breath\\n- Dizziness\\n- Headaches\\n- Poor sleep and snoring\\n- Fever\\n- Weight loss\\n- Nausea\\n- Rare pinkish urine\\n- No perceived recent changes in BP or HR\\n- No medication changes\\n\\nHRV / wearable data provided:\\n- Text snapshot appears to show heart rate sampled every 5 seconds from 2026-02-15 18:30 to 18:51 UTC.\\n- Values appear mostly in the low-to-upper 50s bpm, roughly about 51.3 to 59.9 bpm.\\n- No validated HRV metric (e.g. RMSSD/SDNN) was available from the upload; only pulse-like values were visible in the attached text.\\n\\nWhat I need from you:\\n1) A concise but meaningful differential diagnosis ranked/grouped.\\n2) How the kidney history, hypertension history, rare pink urine, and fever/weight loss alter concern.\\n3) Whether the wearable snapshot changes the assessment much.\\n4) Immediate safety guidance for the patient.\\n5) Keep it suitable for direct relay to the patient on Telegram.\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":250,"output":580,"cacheRead":31360,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":32190,"cost":{"input":0.000625,"output":0.0087,"cacheRead":0.00784,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.017165}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775828157898}}
