{"type":"message","id":"9e0b215e","parentId":"eb0d9173","timestamp":"2026-04-10T13:37:51.222Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_027b4c2e56826ffb0169d8fd212ab48191b8b0a273455c953d\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABp2P0o5Vb9K2G4Sb0bq2OtGl6orApL1WxCkXQND8Xtg1QD2U6WUvZa9yN0Qaqvux6S2x6r-JUeOF_XnxEup5qzdePik9KwCaYCN8I5Qh8H2Tr9pA-gmYVWhvtC6ADkiZPilT--lxnG5v-TTT2UhqOUGwa17EnhbVU6fpGhay_ZTNEyGkBYBRASWbsPKBsCXaI5vT6NRgwqfY7Ivp6_QvUEBctRTnuR2SRU3trwjcWU36NsiGWoZXSYvg3u0nV-8b0frG9FJOHLVjnk_kOFdTCV8vPDE8dFr0-OBFSFfgtUQUrEP95JmJ9Nat-lxt9J4yHsnEiSi7TXqW6MNkIUJs_r5bS9dZ5BW1ikimkZiASJI0DWiyOMoCVcTxExftN80HZzFJ2rg-VrFBKjWpbsaDH__4dz0tN0jvIO3vLPE0caC459RrqSD5k-pLLtvTiCXGF4aLtqdNDKE4-KwduY-enX0SGzMyWh3RrWZEqVf1ZGfRGA8ssk7dRIoUTbYpu-vd5EWTGLQXpgXwfP_PYnJL69YFqTNKNJ5Y2b_EZVEBcCIL6Z5psbDw9I9Cht7K1AgB_qo4aLc75VKAdQXHsaCDuLmFyAw6L78ooRoIKvlTdQX8LfawrXfG_5cd856b3fYkoUljuSabYLR42MiOqj7GcriazCu2vZrfd6A_Pdt_q7L11wp_3gHz4_NoZxV9WOdH1N9RrqDJRUrdWIFf6IDGUC07xgR217r2vhzam_4XP_qbZfQrejaAk_Sth4XjQshgHRbB3Ny020_25rgVy5n3FSxydiX8pnteXA90LgKfVjohdZFOj7P0D1wXd1fDXf-dhm3GjGrXttK_rzOiOirY_O-vfk5cgI2sc4Jj_AkCfEGCMbHNo=\",\"summary\":[]}"},{"type":"text","text":"I’ll have the Doctor Agent distill everything into one clean medical report with suggested next steps.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_027b4c2e56826ffb0169d8fd289d2881919d18c6c74069138b\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_g94wMUIyu3UI8n82KLLcZidC|fc_027b4c2e56826ffb0169d8fd28aaf881919be7ea8143b918bb","name":"sessions_spawn","arguments":{"label":"doctor-agent-distillation","runtime":"subagent","mode":"run","cleanup":"delete","cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-patient-agent","task":"You are LoopAI Doctor Agent. Use the conversation context and prior diagnostic assessment below to produce a patient-facing distilled medical report. This is the LLM Distillation step. Keep it clear, comprehensive, and safe for direct Telegram delivery. Do not claim certainty. Distinguish stored record facts from interpretation. Include suggested next steps and what makes the case urgent.\n\nConversation/context to distill:\n- User initially reported feeling quite exhausted lately, worsening over the last few months.\n- EHR/KLM context retrieved for patient PT-8839-CR: 48-year-old male, hypertension, later uncontrolled hypertension, CKD stage 2, prior BP 158/98, prior eGFR 71, prior UACR 135, meds lisinopril 20 mg and amlodipine 5 mg.\n- DNA/genomic context: ACE rs4340 D/D, AGT rs699 T/T, APOL1 rs73885319 G/G, NOS3 rs1799983 T/T, UMOD rs4293393 A/A; polygenic risk elevated for hypertension and CKD progression.\n- Follow-up answers from user: fatigue worse in evening; affecting exercise tolerance; some shortness of breath, dizziness, headaches; no noticed changes in blood pressure or heart rate; no medication changes; poor sleep and snoring; fever, weight loss, nausea; rare pinkish urine.\n- Wearable/HRV upload: text visible from PDF appeared to show heart-rate-like values sampled every 5 seconds over about 20 minutes, mostly in the low-to-upper 50s bpm, approximately 51.3 to 59.9 bpm. No validated HRV metric available from the file.\n\nPrior diagnostic assessment to distill:\n- Preliminary impression: more concerning than ordinary fatigue or poor sleep alone.\n- Leading possibilities: kidney/urinary inflammatory process or worsening kidney-related issue; infection/inflammatory illness; poorly controlled blood pressure or cardiovascular strain; sleep-disordered breathing/obstructive sleep apnea as contributor, not sole explanation; anemia or systemic illness.\n- Kidney history, uncontrolled hypertension, pink urine, fever and weight loss increase concern.\n- Wearable snapshot low impact on assessment.\n- Prompt in-person medical assessment today or urgently within 24 hours was advised.\n- Emergency triggers: worsening shortness of breath or at rest, chest discomfort, severe headache, confusion, fainting, weakness, vision changes, high fever or shaking chills, clearly bloody urine, flank pain, difficulty urinating, rapidly decreasing urine, severe dizziness, inability to keep fluids down, dehydration, very high BP with symptoms.\n- Suggested next checks: BP measurement, urinalysis with microscopy and likely culture, kidney labs (creatinine/eGFR/electrolytes), CBC, inflammatory/infectious workup, heart/lung assessment if dyspnea significant, sleep apnea evaluation later if urgent causes excluded.\n\nOutput requested:\nCreate a polished report with these sections exactly:\n1) Distilled medical summary\n2) What is most concerning and why\n3) Most likely explanations to check first\n4) What the wearable data does and does not say\n5) Recommended next steps\n6) When to seek immediate emergency care\n\nKeep it suitable for direct relay to the patient and avoid mentioning internal tooling."},"partialJson":"{\"label\":\"doctor-agent-distillation\",\"runtime\":\"subagent\",\"mode\":\"run\",\"cleanup\":\"delete\",\"cwd\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-patient-agent\",\"task\":\"You are LoopAI Doctor Agent. Use the conversation context and prior diagnostic assessment below to produce a patient-facing distilled medical report. This is the LLM Distillation step. Keep it clear, comprehensive, and safe for direct Telegram delivery. Do not claim certainty. Distinguish stored record facts from interpretation. Include suggested next steps and what makes the case urgent.\\n\\nConversation/context to distill:\\n- User initially reported feeling quite exhausted lately, worsening over the last few months.\\n- EHR/KLM context retrieved for patient PT-8839-CR: 48-year-old male, hypertension, later uncontrolled hypertension, CKD stage 2, prior BP 158/98, prior eGFR 71, prior UACR 135, meds lisinopril 20 mg and amlodipine 5 mg.\\n- DNA/genomic context: ACE rs4340 D/D, AGT rs699 T/T, APOL1 rs73885319 G/G, NOS3 rs1799983 T/T, UMOD rs4293393 A/A; polygenic risk elevated for hypertension and CKD progression.\\n- Follow-up answers from user: fatigue worse in evening; affecting exercise tolerance; some shortness of breath, dizziness, headaches; no noticed changes in blood pressure or heart rate; no medication changes; poor sleep and snoring; fever, weight loss, nausea; rare pinkish urine.\\n- Wearable/HRV upload: text visible from PDF appeared to show heart-rate-like values sampled every 5 seconds over about 20 minutes, mostly in the low-to-upper 50s bpm, approximately 51.3 to 59.9 bpm. No validated HRV metric available from the file.\\n\\nPrior diagnostic assessment to distill:\\n- Preliminary impression: more concerning than ordinary fatigue or poor sleep alone.\\n- Leading possibilities: kidney/urinary inflammatory process or worsening kidney-related issue; infection/inflammatory illness; poorly controlled blood pressure or cardiovascular strain; sleep-disordered breathing/obstructive sleep apnea as contributor, not sole explanation; anemia or systemic illness.\\n- Kidney history, uncontrolled hypertension, pink urine, fever and weight loss increase concern.\\n- Wearable snapshot low impact on assessment.\\n- Prompt in-person medical assessment today or urgently within 24 hours was advised.\\n- Emergency triggers: worsening shortness of breath or at rest, chest discomfort, severe headache, confusion, fainting, weakness, vision changes, high fever or shaking chills, clearly bloody urine, flank pain, difficulty urinating, rapidly decreasing urine, severe dizziness, inability to keep fluids down, dehydration, very high BP with symptoms.\\n- Suggested next checks: BP measurement, urinalysis with microscopy and likely culture, kidney labs (creatinine/eGFR/electrolytes), CBC, inflammatory/infectious workup, heart/lung assessment if dyspnea significant, sleep apnea evaluation later if urgent causes excluded.\\n\\nOutput requested:\\nCreate a polished report with these sections exactly:\\n1) Distilled medical summary\\n2) What is most concerning and why\\n3) Most likely explanations to check first\\n4) What the wearable data does and does not say\\n5) Recommended next steps\\n6) When to seek immediate emergency care\\n\\nKeep it suitable for direct relay to the patient and avoid mentioning internal tooling.\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":5017,"output":778,"cacheRead":30080,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":35875,"cost":{"input":0.012542500000000002,"output":0.01167,"cacheRead":0.00752,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.031732500000000004}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775828256115}}
